"(iii) A plaintiff may recover noneconomic losses, including pain
and suffering, emotional distress and loss of enjoyment of property, if the
plaintiff demonstrates by clear and convincing evidence that the electric
utility:
(A) Engaged in gross negligence or willful misconduct in
violation of industry safety standards; or
(B) Failed to take reasonable steps to prevent a wildfire
when a known hazard existed.". LIEN
HB0192H3002/FAILED
Page 10-after line 19 Insert and renumber as necessary:
"(e) An electric utility shall recover not more than eighty percent (80%)
of the total costs of an approved wildfire mitigation plan through rate
adjustments to consumers. Not less than twenty percent (20%) of the costs shall
be borne by the electric utility to ensure financial accountability and
incentive-based risk management.". LIEN
